+## Choosing which tools agents can use
+
+In a hosted app's **Tools** tab, app managers can turn individual tools or whole
+groups off for everyone using that app. Switched-off tools disappear from agent
+search and listings, and calls to their old paths are refused. Other apps and
+saved accounts keep their own access.
+
+Use **Show hidden tools** to find and restore a switched-off tool. **Turn off all
+writes** keeps tools off unless their metadata explicitly marks them read-only;
+new write tools stay off after upgrades too. You can turn on individual exceptions
+or restore all writes. Enabling a tool keeps its existing permission and approval
+checks.
+
+Agents can read these settings and ask to change them through the built-in
+management app's `toolAvailability` tools, including over MCP. Changes require
+the same app management authority and use the normal approval flow.
+
